  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The required height of a TV tower which can cover the population of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math>&nbsp;lakh is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>. If the average population density is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>per square <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi></math> and the radius of earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Maximum range of TV transmission&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math>&nbsp;(here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>)</p><p>Maximum area of TV transmission</p><p>Area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>km</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
